---
description: Guardrails against regressions when editing this repo
alwaysApply: true
---

# No regression

- Before finishing any change: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm lint && pnpm test && pnpm build`
  must all pass.
- Never remove or bypass these behaviours without explicit instruction:
  - Room create/join/rejoin flow and 4-char room codes.
  - Host migration when the host disconnects.
  - The authoritative-server model (clients send intents only).
  - The reveal event queue (no silent score changes).
  - Score-gap/rank-aware power-up odds and the active arcade power-up catalogue.
  - Secret mutiny declaration and private-state isolation.
  - The debug/playtest panel in dev mode (and its absence in production).
- When simplifying a mechanic, keep it playable and update the implementation mismatch/TODO in
  `docs/context/MECHANICS.md` — never silently drop or relabel a mechanic.
- Do not rename socket event names without updating both client and server plus
  `shared/src/types/index.ts` (`ClientEvents`/`ServerEvents`).
- Keep `pnpm dev` working end-to-end: two browser windows must be able to play a full game
  locally after any change.
